Project: Mystery Machine - fan project and legal notice
=======================================================

Unofficial fan project
----------------------

Project: Mystery Machine is an unofficial, non-commercial fan project: a
native Windows port of Scooby-Doo! Night of 100 Frights, built from a
decompilation of the GameCube release. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by
or endorsed by Warner Bros. Discovery, Hanna-Barbera, Cartoon Network, THQ,
Heavy Iron Studios or Nintendo.

Scooby-Doo! Night of 100 Frights, Scooby-Doo, the Mystery Machine and all
related characters, names, music, artwork and logos are trademarks and/or
copyrights of their respective owners. All rights remain with them.

No game data
------------

Neither the source repository nor the release archive contains game data: no
disc image, no extracted files, no models, textures, audio, video, text or
level data. You need your own copy of the game (USA, disc ID GIHE78) and must
dump your own disc; that is your responsibility under your local law.

Decompiled game code
--------------------

The sources under src/, include/ and config/ are derived from the retail game
for study and for building a matching binary. They remain the copyright of the
game's owners. Nothing here grants you a licence to them, to the game, or to
any character.

Launcher artwork (third-party, personal use only)
-------------------------------------------------

The launcher's header badge and its icon use a Scooby-Doo portrait, and its
header uses a Mystery Machine van, taken from free PNG clip-art sites. Those
sites offer the files for personal, non-commercial use only and state that the
depicted characters remain the property of their owners:

  - Scooby-Doo portrait (header badge, and the source of launcher.ico):
    "Scooby Doo Cartoon Character PNG", pngall.com
  - Mystery Machine van (header): "The Mystery Machine", stickpng.com

These two images, and the .ico rendered from the portrait, are NOT covered by
the project's CC0 licence and are NOT licensed to you for redistribution,
reuse or commercial use. They must not be extracted and republished on their
own. They are included only so the launcher can be built and used as it looks;
the compiled scooby_launcher.exe embeds them as resources.

Building from source without them is supported: delete pc/launcher/scooby.png,
pc/launcher/van.png and pc/launcher/launcher.ico and launcher.cpp draws its own
Great Dane badge (and, if van.png is missing, its own van) instead.

